WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.513 --> 00:00:03.720
- [Narrator] What's the
highest you've ever slept at?

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.192
- [Mark] Almost a mile.

00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:07.560
When you don't have a fear of heights,

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.042
it's not really scary.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.434
It's like being in the craziest tree house

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:14.335
that you could possibly imagine.

00:00:14.335 --> 00:00:15.416
- [Narrator] That's Mark Sinnett.

00:00:15.416 --> 00:00:16.674
He's a professional rock climber,

00:00:16.674 --> 00:00:19.088
and he's talking about sleeping in a tent.

00:00:19.088 --> 00:00:19.921
- [Mark] They're called portaledges.

00:00:19.921 --> 00:00:23.110
- [Narrator] That's hanging
off the side of a mountain.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:25.098
He's been climbing for over 30 years,

00:00:25.098 --> 00:00:29.339
and his favorite walls to
climb are really, really high.

00:00:29.339 --> 00:00:33.657
- [Mark] Alpine big wall
climbing is the pursuit

00:00:33.657 --> 00:00:38.164
of scaling the biggest
cliffs on planet earth.

00:00:38.164 --> 00:00:41.617
- [Narrator] They take
a few days to summit.

00:00:41.617 --> 00:00:43.697
So he has to camp out along the way.

00:00:43.697 --> 00:00:46.092
So I want to know what does it feel like

00:00:46.092 --> 00:00:48.940
to sleep in a portaledge hanging off

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.857
the side of a mountain?

00:00:52.202 --> 00:00:54.791
- [Mark] The one thing that's
more or less ever present

00:00:54.791 --> 00:00:58.958
in the mountains is when
it can be pretty violent.

00:01:01.515 --> 00:01:04.932
You can experience hurricane force winds,

00:01:06.015 --> 00:01:10.977
there's also this thing that
we call the Bronco ride.

00:01:10.977 --> 00:01:13.319
Wind comes in, hits a cliff,

00:01:13.319 --> 00:01:16.369
and it really has nowhere
to go except for up.

00:01:16.369 --> 00:01:18.706
Eventually it hits you and your ledge

00:01:18.706 --> 00:01:21.000
and it can lift the whole thing off

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.169
so you can be suspended
and then, of course,

00:01:25.169 --> 00:01:28.064
the ledge like slams into the wall.

00:01:28.064 --> 00:01:29.932
You're just thinking about surviving.

00:01:29.932 --> 00:01:32.908
- [Narrator] And that
wasn't the worst of it.

00:01:32.908 --> 00:01:36.575
- [Mark] The smell in
the ledge is not nice.

00:01:37.827 --> 00:01:39.224
You don't change your clothes,

00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:40.557
you don't bathe.

00:01:41.887 --> 00:01:43.637
It's wet, it's gummy.

00:01:45.287 --> 00:01:46.687
- [Narrator] But people love it.

00:01:46.687 --> 00:01:48.733
They continue to climb and explore

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:51.089
through all of this punishment

00:01:51.089 --> 00:01:53.750
because there's still
that one question left:

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.762
How does it feel?

00:01:55.762 --> 00:01:57.438
- [Mark] The way it makes you feel

00:01:57.438 --> 00:01:59.855
is like a tiny speck of dust.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:03.949
It's very empowering.

00:02:03.949 --> 00:02:08.187
It really is just kind of
like the most spectacular spot

00:02:08.187 --> 00:02:10.980
that you can be on planet earth.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.730
(peaceful music)

